The maximum probationary period is 6 months, counted from the date the employee starts work. This comes from Article 9(1) of Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, and an employer cannot put the same employee on probation again once that period is over. I found no amendment that changes this cap, but I only checked secondary sources such as news sites and law-firm summaries, not the official consolidated text from MOHRE.

Sources: [Khaleej Times](https://www.khaleejtimes.com/legal/uae-jobs-what-you-need-to-know-about-6-month-probation-period-after-new-employment-law-went-into-fo), [Gulf News](https://gulfnews.com/living-in-uae/ask-us/new-uae-labour-law-what-are-your-rights-during-probation-period-1.1637159316752), [Water and Shark](https://www.waterandshark.com/blog/uae-labour-law)

