A worker on probation who ends the contract to work for another employer in the UAE must give the current employer **at least one month's written notice**. That rule is in **Article 9(3) of Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021**, and unless agreed otherwise, the new employer must pay the original employer's recruitment costs. A worker leaving the UAE altogether needs only 14 days' notice under Article 9(4); I quoted Article 9(3) from memory because I couldn't open the official MOHRE text to confirm that later amendments haven't changed it.

Sources: [MOHRE – Decree-Law 33/2021 and its amendments](https://www.mohre.gov.ae/assets/download/3bde4984/Federal%20Decree-Law%20No.%2033%20of%202021%20Regarding%20the%20Regulation%20of%20Employment%20Relationship%20and%20its%20amendments_638990571068264034.pdf.aspx) (could not be opened); [Gulf News – probation rights](https://gulfnews.com/ask-gulf-news/ask-gulf-news-7-key-rules-and-employee-rights-during-probation-period-in-the-uae-1.500331994)

