A worker on probation who wants to end the contract in order to leave the UAE must give the employer at least 14 days' written notice under Article 9(4) of Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021. This is different from moving to another UAE employer, which requires one month's notice under Article 9(3). If the worker leaves without following these rules, Article 9(6) can bar them from getting a UAE work permit for one year (subject to exceptions); my search didn't bring up the official text of Article 9, but the sources agree on the 14 days.

Sources: [MOHRE – Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021 (English)](https://mohre.gov.ae/assets/download/c93e7702/federal-decree-law-no-33-of-2021-eng.aspx); [The Law Reporters – Probation Period under UAE Labour Law](https://thelawreporters.com/probation-period-under-uae-labour-law-statutory-rights-employer-obligations-and-termination-rules-explained); [Gulf News – Probation period rights](https://gulfnews.com/amp/living-in-uae/ask-us/probation-period-in-the-uae--7-rights-and-responsibilities-you-need-to-know-about-1.1669303233967)

