The gratuity for each of the first five years of service is 21 days' basic wage, rising to 30 days for each year after that. This is set by Article 51 of Federal Decree-Law No. 33 of 2021, and the employee must have at least one year of continuous service to qualify. One law-firm note says the Arabic text may mean 21 *working* days rather than calendar days, and I didn't check the official text myself, but the number of days is 21 either way.

Sources: [UAE Government portal – End of service benefits](https://beta.government.ae/en/information-and-services/jobs/end-of-service-benefits-for-employees-in-the-private-sector); [Gulf News – How is gratuity calculated](https://gulfnews.com/living-in-uae/ask-us/new-uae-labour-law-how-is-gratuity-calculated-1.1639493834258); [Afridi & Angell – End of service gratuity clarified](https://afridi-angell.com/end-of-service-gratuity-clarified/)

