The maximum probationary period is 180 days in total. This comes from Article 53 of the Saudi Labor Law as amended by Royal Decree No. M/44 (1446H), in force since 19 February 2025. The old rule was 90 days, extendable to 180 only by written agreement; now probation must simply be written into the contract with its length, may not exceed 180 days, and either party may end the contract during it.

Sources: [DLA Piper](https://knowledge.dlapiper.com/dlapiperknowledge/globalemploymentlatestdevelopments/2024/Amendments-to-the-KSA-Labour-Law), [Rödl & Partner](https://www.roedl.com/insights/saudi-arabia-labor-law-amendments-impact), [Morgan Lewis](https://www.morganlewis.com/de/pubs/2024/08/key-amendments-to-the-kingdom-of-saudi-arabia-labour-law-announced), [The National](https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/money/2024/10/30/saudi-arabia-labour-law-what/)

